text:
The year is 2033. The Valve Corporation have established themselves as dominant global authority. Everybody in the world is under their control, brainwashed into blind obedience by countless Summer Sales and Steam Workshop mods to all their favourite games. Those with the willpower strong enough to break free are hunted down by Valve's military police force, the SMP and are either killed where they stand or forcibly used to power the Steam servers with their powerful minds. On the 3rd of March, 2033, E3 has finally begun. The mindless zombies wander around, observing the newest developments in their favourite franchises, now all owned by Valve and used to further their wicked agenda. A special event is listed for 0333 hours. The SMP usher every attendee into the main conference hall. Those too weak, poor or frail to make the pilgrimage watched from their computer screens. For three whole minutes, the screen has nothing but the Steam insignia on it. Then, all of a sudden, a hydraulic hiss is heard. All eyes are fixated at the front of the room. The walls open up and, escorted by a group of powerful Steam Moderators, an elegant, dark shape is taken onto the stage. A pure aura of brilliance emanates off his beautiful form. It can only be one person; Lord Gaben, The Supreme Leader, Bringer of the Great Summer Sale. The billion-strong crowd roars with approval, jumping up and down, trying to reach Gaben to get a whiff of his glorious musk, only to be pushed back by SMP officers. A man passes Lord Gaben a microphone, his demeanor suggesting he thought himself unworthy. After clearing his throat, he leans as far as he can towards the mic and says one thing;
"Half-Life 3 is to be released immediately."
The sheer amazement of the crowd overrides their minds. They simply move like clockwork to their homes, to get to their computers. Those who are at home instantly open the Steam App and purchase it. Everyone on Earth was now fully under the control of Lord Gaben. As he is escorted back to his palace, he smirks, saying one last thing;
"I hope it was worth the wait."
10/10 game.

