Since I am a great fan of Terraria (about 400 hourse played), after having got all the top loot and studied the game from A to Z, I wanted to play something just as amazing as Terraria, which could hold me for another couple hundred of hourse.So here it is -- Starbound.Actually, it is the same Terraria but with blackjack and hookers...and spaceships(c).The potential of Starbound is just magnificent  comparing again with  Terraria: endless amount of self-generating maps (planets indeed); wide spectre of characters as in the environment (NPCs) as for playing like a main character with its pluses and minuses depending on race you chose; loot for any taste etc.
PROS:
- great variety of everything;
- pixel-art as it is;
- nice potential for upgrating/updating/promotion;
- craft system;
- kind of unic gameplay which possibly will not get you tired;
- who knows what cool sweets are going to be brought into the game by the depelopers?
CONS:
- not the most attractive price (still  worths it, belive me);
- the game is still in betta-stage and it's for long probably;
- it's good for you to play already, but be carefull: all loot/progress you have got will be deleted with releasing a new global patch.
Verdict: Starbound is an AMAZING representator of its genre and doubtlessly one of the best sandboxes nowadays and further.The only question is will  Terraria 2 be able to become equal  finished Starbound!
Thanks a lot for your attention!
Madrocker.

