Running from Xubuntu 17.04 client on ASUS X206HA.
Pros:
_relatively short (main story completed in 8h with a few achievements) but with a clear progression and already a decent variety of tasks;
_nice soundtracks and visuals;
_the miscellaneous files spread over the machines, feeling like NPCs;
_runs smoothly on low-end computer;
Cons:
_the net-map becomes quite messy in the end
Suggestions:
_improved auto-completion for, among others, relative paths more than one branch away from current directory;
_extended interpretation of star symbol, e.g. running commands like "rm *.txt";
_multiple commands separated by semicolon (but it may break part of the tension);
_adding x-server themes, adding miscellaneous files to make machines more realistic, maybe adding a basic editor instead of the "replace" command;
_replace the net-map by a table of IP-hostname-login-passwd?
_countless times I've been hitting "ctrl+a" and "ctrl+e" to navigate faster in the narrow console area, "ctrl+c" to quickly interrupt the current line, "ctrl+d" to quickly log out... these could be useful additions
I guess the console-only mission can be suddenly hard for non-unix users, but at the same time the shell would be perfect if the entire game could be run in console mode =)

